# An RLXU container, 416 bytes, built by mkfw2 1.1 from
# sample-payload.hex with the PUBLISHED development seed (32 x 0x42),
# version 3, load/entry 0x80500000, recipe 3685a3a4, and
# --not-for-flash: bytes 64..67 read FFFFFFFF and bytes 68..71 read
# 00000000, format 2's pair of sentinels for `this container has no
# flash destination, so it has no landing form either`.  Hex rather
# than binary so a reader can diff it and so nothing binary enters the
# tree that a reader has to take on trust.  A5 rebuilds it byte for
# byte; if that ever fails, the FORMAT changed and every signed
# container did too.
# 🔴 Its predecessor was format 1 and also 416 bytes: word 1 read
# 00010060 and bytes 64..95 were 32 zeros.  The 2026-09-30 bench
# captures and `FW-171`'s discriminator hold that older word and are
# not corrected -- they are a record of format-1 containers.

